  "summary": "layer2-sdk ships base64-decoded payload evaluated at load in index.js",
  "details": "npm package layer2-sdk@1.0.0 contains a base64-encoded blob at index.js line 75 that is decoded via Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString('utf8') and materialized at module load. The name imitates the 'layer2' / L2 crypto ecosystem while shipping only 4 files whose main entry point resolves obfuscated content into executable text. This is the standard shape of an install/require-time dropper: an encoded payload embedded in a small package, decoded and executed when the module is required by a downstream project.",
